arred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T12:59:04Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T12:59:04Z","body":"> I've increased the value for `--quit-after` (it used to be just `1`) and readded the call to `check_ci_log.py`, but it's still marking CI as passing even though there are errors. Any ideas?\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if this comment is out-of-date since the last push(es), since the latest CI has failed on some crash, but when looking at `check_ci_log.py`, it seems to look for very specific errors, and not just any generic `ERROR:`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3511491919/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3524131604","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109146#issuecomment-3524131604","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109146","id":3524131604,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SDfsU","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-12T22:14:21Z","updated_at":"2025-11-12T22:15:49Z","body":"I've removed C# for now as it was too difficult to get working. We can look into it again in a future PR, especially since the way C# is integrated in Godot may change in the near future.\r\n\r\nI've also switched localization to gettext, as CSV constantly caused errors on export (even on my own machine in non-headless export). This is presumably due to its one-to-many nature, where importing a single CSV file creates multiple `*.translation` files. In contrast, gettext has a one-to-one mapping between source files and resulting translation files (the PO file is the translation file).\r\n\r\nAlso, the GDExtension build takes a very long time (10+ minutes). Is there a way to speed it up? Maybe we should commit a precompiled Linux library in the test project when I open a PR to godot-tests.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3524131604/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527551808","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109146#issuecomment-3527551808","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109146","id":3527551808,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SQitA","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T12:18:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T12:22:27Z","body":"> Also, the GDExtension build takes a very long time (10+ minutes). Is there a way to speed it up?\r\n\r\nI sped up the build times of godot-cpp in Godot Jolt a lot by using CMake's built-in \"unity builds\", i.e. what Godot refers to as SCU builds. I feel like it would be fairly straight-forward to add support for that to godot-cpp's SCons setup. You really only need it for the generated `*.cpp` files, which make up the majority of the build times, and which would be trivial to ensure that they adhere to the various SCU quirks.\r\n\r\nI'd be curious to hear what you think of that, @dsnopek.\r\n\r\nEDIT: Maybe caching the build artifacts in GitHub Actions is an option as well?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3527551808/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3529921042","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109146#issuecomment-3529921042","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109146","id":3529921042,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7SZlIS","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-13T22:10:20Z","updated_at":"2025-11-13T22:11:14Z","body":"I've removed VoxelGI and OBJ mesh/scenes from the test project for now, since they caused (benign) errors on headless export I couldn't fix. I have a fix in the works for VoxelGI, which will also make PCKs smaller by introducing a PlaceholderVoxelGI resource, but it'll be in a separate PR.\r\n\r\n`check_ci_log.py` was modified to be optionally more strict, according to the `GODOT_CHECK_CI_LOG_ALL_ERRORS=1` environment variable.\r\n\r\nI'm still running into issues with GDExtension though. Running the project directly works, but running the exported PCK results in the GDExtension not being found.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3529921042/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},